# Normalise every text file to LF, in the repository and in working copies.
#
# Not cosmetic. A theme may bundle plugins (`manifest.plugins`), and `alvyth:plugin-sign`
# signs a SHA-256 digest of every file's contents. With `core.autocrlf=true` — the Windows
# default, and what this project is developed on — git hands a Windows checkout CRLF and a
# Linux checkout LF, so the same commit produces two different digests and a package signed
# on one machine fails verification after being cloned on the other. Pinning the line ending
# is what makes the signature reproducible from source.
#
# It matters for the theme's own files too: `ThemeController` resolves Blade templates from
# the deployed tree, and a diff that is nothing but line endings buries every real change.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touched by line-ending conversion.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
*.zip binary
*.pem binary
plugin.sig binary
